3) Creator dashboard misses required metric: top scan hours.
- UI now shows total/7d/30d, trend chart, platform breakdown, and verdict breakdown.
- But there is no rendering of `topHours`, despite backend summary producing it and task explicitly requiring “top scan hours”.

4) API versioning is incomplete for required routes.
- New `/api/v1` routers include validate-email, decode-image, qr active, donation, and analytics.
- Required moved routes included `/safe-browsing` and `/analyze` (and explicit new `POST /api/v1/analyze` from Phase 2).
- Neither appears in `server/routes/security.ts` or `server/routes/index.ts`.

5) Aggregation “all-time” can be wrong at scale.
- Both client/service and server analytics endpoints cap reads at 2000 events and report `totalScans = eventsSnap.size/docs.length`.
- This is not true all-time once >2000 events.

Security: none observed that are severe and task-blocking. Owner auth is enforced on `GET /api/v1/qr/:uuid/analytics` and `PATCH /api/v1/qr/:qrId/active`.

Next actions:
1) Complete event contract and coverage: add `country` collection (non-PII), and ensure all successful scan paths (including guard/standard URL paths and anonymous mode) call `recordScanEvent` fire-and-forget.
2) Add missing v1 endpoints (`/api/v1/analyze`, safe-browsing equivalent) and keep unversioned compatibility paths as intended.
3) Implement top scan hours section in `MyQrAnalyticsScreen` and correct all-time totals (use authoritative counter or full aggregation strategy).